  "summary": "npm package auto-executes bundled Windows binary loading virus.jar on install",
  "details": "package.json declares a postinstall hook `.\\DakuMangalSingh\\DakuMangalSingh.exe` that runs automatically on `npm install` on Windows. The bundled executable is a jpackage launcher configured to load `app/virus.jar` (main class `Main`). The JAR archive is explicitly named `virus.jar` and ships classes `Main`, `Executor`, `Fetch`, `RobotService`, `Screenshort`, and `DeviceId` — the structural shape of a remote command executor, screen-capture module, and host fingerprinter. The package has empty name/author/description/license metadata and no library surface: its only function is to deliver and auto-execute the bundled payload at install time.",
